  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 2925bd0c6a5ea9a4fbbc9ab434791dc5, type: 3}
  m_Name: Disease_PotatoEarlyBlight
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  diseaseId: early_blight
  diseaseName: Early Blight
  aiLabelAliases:
  - Potato___Early_blight
  - potato_early_blight
  - potato early blight
  - Potato leaf early blight
  pathogenType: 0
  pathogen: 
  affectedPart: 0
  sources: []
  description: A common fungal leaf disease of potato caused by Alternaria solani.
  causes: Warm, humid weather with long leaf wetness; stressed or under-fed plants;
    inoculum on crop debris.
  effectOnPlant: Lesions destroy leaf area and weaken the plant late in the season.
  untreatedOutcome: Early defoliation reduces tuber size and yield.
  symptoms:
  - Dark spots with concentric target rings
  - Yellowing around spots
  - Older, lower leaves first
  supportingFeatureIds:
  - leaf_spots
  - yellowing
  - leaf_color
  moderateSeverityThreshold: 0.35
  severeSeverityThreshold: 0.7
  treatmentPlan: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 855929e7b601b054daf14f62c7cea2ff, type: 2}
  preventionPlan: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 3251d71b260c58d4f90034e44d606fba, type: 2}
  simulationProfile: {fileID: 11400000, guid: f56b192df71496341bac1dd8b8b57c3d, type: 2}
  lifecycleStages:
  - Spores survive on crop debris and in the soil between seasons.
  - Wind and splashing water carry them to the lower, older leaves.
  - Dark spots with rings and yellow halos appear within days in warm, damp weather.
  - Spots join, leaves yellow and drop, and new spores spread to nearby plants.
  conditionFactors:
  - "Warm days, roughly 24\u201329 \xB0C, with humid nights."
  - Leaves staying wet from dew, rain or overhead watering.
  - Older or stressed plants, especially those short of nitrogen.
  - Plants close together, or infected debris left on the ground.
  referencePhotos:
  - {fileID: 2800000, guid: 8f498da233d0dee4e86a5a273387afaa, type: 3}
  lesionLabel: Ringed lesion
  haloLabel: Yellow halo
  areaLabel: Yellowing leaf
